  "question": {
    "text": "The reduction of peroxydisulphate ion by I ion\r\n\r\nis expressed by $\\mathrm{S}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{8}^{2-}+3 \\mathrm{I}^{-} \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{SO}_{4}^{2-}+\\mathrm{I}_{3}^{-}$. If\r\n\r\nrate of disappearance of $\\mathrm{I}^{-}$ is $9 / 2 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~mol}$ lit $^{-1}$\r\n\r\n$\\mathrm{s}^{-1},$ what is the rate of formation of $2 \\mathrm{SO}_{4}^{2-}$ during same time?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$3 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~mol} \\mathrm{Lit}^{-1} \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$2 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~mol} \\mathrm{Lit}^{-1} \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$10^{-3} \\mathrm{~mol} \\mathrm{Lit}^{-1} \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$4 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~mol} \\mathrm{Lit}^{-1} \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\frac{1 d\\left[\\mathrm{SO}_{4}^{2-}\\right]}{2}=\\frac{1}{3}\\left(-\\frac{\\mathrm{d}\\left(\\mathrm{I}^{-}\\right)}{d t}\\right)$\r\n\r\n$\\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{d\\left[\\mathrm{SO}_{4}^{2-}\\right]}{d t}=\\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{9}{2} \\times 10^{-3}$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore \\quad \\frac{d\\left[\\mathrm{SO}_{4}^{2-}\\right]}{d t}=3 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~mol} \\mathrm{Lit}^{-1} \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$"
  }
}